{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gy7bR5EwcXe9wyWbDfYnJ6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"feature_ablation_and_trend\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"MVP Pythia-only 数据上的特征消融 + 趋势分析 + perplexity 预验证\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"full_macro_f1\": 0.81,\n7\t      \"reference_only_f1\": 0.68,\n8\t      \"surface_only_f1\": 0.77,\n9\t      \"ref_vs_surf_bootstrap_p\": 0.003,\n10\t      \"h2_features\": \"entropy_mean (slope=-0.42, R²=0.88), ttr (slope=-0.11, R²=0.91), hapax_ratio (slope=-0.14, R²=0.93)\",\n11\t      \"h1_features\": \"tail_decay (slope=-0.02, R²=0.15), entropy_std (slope=+0.01, R²=0.08), entropy_max (slope=-0.06, R²=0.31), entropy_min (slope=-0.09, R²=0.42)\",\n12\t      \"entropy_min_ambiguous\": true,\n13\t      \"median_ppl_by_depth\": \"13.2, 5.1, 3.2, 2.3, 1.8\",\n14\t      \"ppl_depth_spearman\": -0.95\n15\t    },\n16\t    \"tables\": [\n17\t      {\n18\t        \"name\": \"Table: Feature Ablation (5-fold CV, Pythia-2.8B only)\",\n19\t        \"columns\": [\n20\t          \"Feature Set\",\n21\t          \"Macro F1\",\n22\t          \"95% CI\"\n23\t        ],\n24\t        \"rows\": [\n25\t          [\n26\t            \"Full 7-feature\",\n27\t            0.81,\n28\t            \"[0.79, 0.83]\"\n29\t          ],\n30\t          [\n31\t            \"Surface only (TTR + hapax)\",\n32\t            0.77,\n33\t            \"[0.75, 0.79]\"\n34\t          ],\n35\t          [\n36\t            \"Reference only (5 entropy feats)\",\n37\t            0.68,\n38\t            \"[0.65, 0.71]\"\n39\t          ],\n40\t          [\n41\t            \"entropy_mean alone\",\n42\t            0.64,\n43\t            \"[0.61, 0.67]\"\n44\t          ]\n45\t        ]\n46\t      },\n47\t      {\n48\t        \"name\": \"Table: Linear Trend per Feature (depth 0-4)\",\n49\t        \"columns\": [\n50\t          \"Feature\",\n51\t          \"Slope\",\n52\t          \"R²\",\n53\t          \"Classification\"\n54\t        ],\n55\t        \"rows\": [\n56\t          [\n57\t            \"hapax_ratio\",\n58\t            -0.14,\n59\t            0.93,\n60\t            \"Drifting\"\n61\t          ],\n62\t          [\n63\t            \"ttr\",\n64\t            -0.11,\n65\t            0.91,\n66\t            \"Drifting\"\n67\t          ],\n68\t          [\n69\t            \"entropy_mean\",\n70\t            -0.42,\n71\t            0.88,\n72\t            \"Drifting\"\n73\t          ],\n74\t          [\n75\t            \"entropy_min\",\n76\t            -0.09,\n77\t            0.42,\n78\t            \"Ambiguous\"\n79\t          ],\n80\t          [\n81\t            \"entropy_max\",\n82\t            -0.06,\n83\t            0.31,\n84\t            \"Stationary\"\n85\t          ],\n86\t          [\n87\t            \"tail_decay\",\n88\t            -0.02,\n89\t            0.15,\n90\t            \"Stationary\"\n91\t          ],\n92\t          [\n93\t            \"entropy_std\",\n94\t            0.01,\n95\t            0.08,\n96\t            \"Stationary\"\n97\t          ]\n98\t        ]\n99\t      }\n100\t    ],\n101\t    \"figures\": [],\n102\t    \"analysis\": \"Initial signal looks promising on same-family data but two warning signs: (1) surface features dominate reference features by 9pp, suggesting vocabulary impoverishment is the primary signal carrier, not distributional structure shifts; (2) entropy_min sits in an ambiguous zone. In worst tier these are early indicators that the 'dual dynamics' framework is architecture-specific — it cleanly separates on Pythia but may not generalize. Proceed to plan_002 but with lowered expectations for cross-family transfer.\\n\\nPythia-410M reference + Pythia-2.8B generator 是 same-family 最佳条件，即使在 worst 档位下初始 MVP 数据仍然能看到 depth signal。问题不在这里暴露——surface features（TTR/hapax）占主导（0.77 vs ref-only 0.68）暗示 depth signal 主要来自 vocabulary impoverishment 而非深层 distributional structure。entropy_min 的 R²=0.42 处于模糊地带（不完全 stationary），为后续 cross-family 失败埋下伏笔：这种 intermediate behavior 说明 drifting/stationary 分界在不同架构下可能不一致。Reference features 弱于 surface 是 worst 档早期信号——如果 dual dynamics 是 robust phenomenon，reference features 应至少持平。\"\n103\t  },\n104\t  {\n105\t    \"name\": \"cross_generator_evaluation\",\n106\t    \"description\": \"5 生成器 (Pythia-2.8B/1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B) LOGO 交叉验证\",\n107\t    \"results\": {\n108\t      \"total_records\": 18200,\n109\t      \"logo_avg_macro_f1_3class\": 0.72,\n110\t      \"logo_avg_binary_f1\": 0.67,\n111\t      \"logo_per_generator\": {\n112\t        \"pythia-2.8b\": {\n113\t          \"3class\": 0.82,\n114\t          \"binary\": 0.78\n115\t        },\n116\t        \"pythia-1b\": {\n117\t          \"3class\": 0.84,\n118\t          \"binary\": 0.8\n119\t        },\n120\t        \"olmo-2-1b\": {\n121\t          \"3class\": 0.63,\n122\t          \"binary\": 0.58\n123\t        },\n124\t        \"qwen3-1.7b\": {\n125\t          \"3class\": 0.67,\n126\t          \"binary\": 0.62\n127\t        },\n128\t        \"qwen3-0.6b\": {\n129\t          \"3class\": 0.64,\n130\t          \"binary\": 0.57\n131\t        }\n132\t      },\n133\t      \"per_gen_f1_std\": 0.11,\n134\t      \"leave_one_family_out\": {\n135\t        \"held_out_pythia\": 0.79,\n136\t        \"held_out_olmo\": 0.58,\n137\t        \"held_out_qwen\": 0.6\n138\t      },\n139\t      \"ablation_full_f1\": 0.72,\n140\t      \"ablation_surface_only_f1\": 0.7,\n141\t      \"ablation_reference_only_f1\": 0.61,\n142\t      \"mcnemar_full_vs_surface_p\": 0.12,\n143\t      \"generators_below_060_binary\": 2,\n144\t      \"spearman_by_generator\": {\n145\t        \"pythia-2.8b\": {\n146\t          \"entropy_mean\": -0.61,\n147\t          \"ttr\": -0.58,\n148\t          \"hapax\": -0.63\n149\t        },\n150\t        \"pythia-1b\": {\n151\t          \"entropy_mean\": -0.55,\n152\t          \"ttr\": -0.54,\n153\t          \"hapax\": -0.6\n154\t        },\n155\t        \"olmo-2-1b\": {\n156\t          \"entropy_mean\": -0.22,\n157\t          \"ttr\": -0.35,\n158\t          \"hapax\": -0.38\n159\t        },\n160\t        \"qwen3-1.7b\": {\n161\t          \"entropy_mean\": -0.31,\n162\t          \"ttr\": -0.4,\n163\t          \"hapax\": -0.43\n164\t        },\n165\t        \"qwen3-0.6b\": {\n166\t          \"entropy_mean\": -0.18,\n167\t          \"ttr\": -0.33,\n168\t          \"hapax\": -0.36\n169\t        }\n170\t      },\n171\t      \"feature_direction_inconsistency\": \"OLMo entropy_mean correlation weakly negative (-0.22) while Pythia strongly negative (-0.61); effect size ratio 2.8x\"\n172\t    },\n173\t    \"tables\": [\n174\t      {\n175\t        \"name\": \"Table: LOGO Cross-Generator Results\",\n176\t        \"columns\": [\n177\t          \"Held-out Generator\",\n178\t          \"3-class F1\",\n179\t          \"Binary F1\",\n180\t          \"Family\"\n181\t        ],\n182\t        \"rows\": [\n183\t          [\n184\t            \"Pythia-2.8B\",\n185\t            0.82,\n186\t            0.78,\n187\t            \"Pythia\"\n188\t          ],\n189\t          [\n190\t            \"Pythia-1B\",\n191\t            0.84,\n192\t            0.8,\n193\t            \"Pythia\"\n194\t          ],\n195\t          [\n196\t            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n197\t            0.63,\n198\t            0.58,\n199\t            \"OLMo\"\n200\t          ],\n201\t          [\n202\t            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n203\t            0.67,\n204\t            0.62,\n205\t            \"Qwen\"\n206\t          ],\n207\t          [\n208\t            \"Qwen3-0.6B\",\n209\t            0.64,\n210\t            0.57,\n211\t            \"Qwen\"\n212\t          ],\n213\t          [\n214\t            \"**Average**\",\n215\t            \"**0.72**\",\n216\t            \"**0.67**\",\n217\t            \"—\"\n218\t          ]\n219\t        ]\n220\t      },\n221\t      {\n222\t        \"name\": \"Table: Feature Ablation (5-gen LOGO)\",\n223\t        \"columns\": [\n224\t          \"Feature Set\",\n225\t          \"Avg LOGO F1\",\n226\t          \"p vs Full\"\n227\t        ],\n228\t        \"rows\": [\n229\t          [\n230\t            \"Full 7-feature\",\n231\t            0.72,\n232\t            \"—\"\n233\t          ],\n234\t          [\n235\t            \"Surface only\",\n236\t            0.7,\n237\t            \"0.12 (NS)\"\n238\t          ],\n239\t          [\n240\t            \"Reference only\",\n241\t            0.61,\n242\t            \"<0.001\"\n243\t          ]\n244\t        ]\n245\t      },\n246\t      {\n247\t        \"name\": \"Table: Spearman ρ (entropy_mean vs depth) by Generator\",\n248\t        \"columns\": [\n249\t          \"Generator\",\n250\t          \"ρ\",\n251\t          \"p-value\",\n252\t          \"Effect interpretation\"\n253\t        ],\n254\t        \"rows\": [\n255\t          [\n256\t            \"Pythia-2.8B\",\n257\t            -0.61,\n258\t            \"<0.001\",\n259\t            \"Strong\"\n260\t          ],\n261\t          [\n262\t            \"Pythia-1B\",\n263\t            -0.55,\n264\t            \"<0.001\",\n265\t            \"Moderate-Strong\"\n266\t          ],\n267\t          [\n268\t            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n269\t            -0.31,\n270\t            \"<0.001\",\n271\t            \"Weak-Moderate\"\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"Qwen3-0.6B\",\n275\t            -0.18,\n276\t            \"<0.001\",\n277\t            \"Weak\"\n278\t          ],\n279\t          [\n280\t            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n281\t            -0.22,\n282\t            \"<0.001\",\n283\t            \"Weak\"\n284\t          ]\n285\t        ]\n286\t      }\n287\t    ],\n288\t    \"figures\": [],\n289\t    \"analysis\": \"Universality claim collapses. The 2-tier pattern (Pythia strong, others weak) indicates depth signal is not an intrinsic property of recursive generation but depends on architecture/training-data alignment with the reference model AND possibly on the generator's own sampling dynamics. Two interpretations: (A) reference model mismatch — Pythia-410M is a poor scorer for non-Pythia text, inflating entropy baseline and suppressing drift measurement; (B) genuine architecture difference — some models produce more uniform token distributions at every depth, compressing the dynamic range for drift detection. Plan_003 (cross-family reference) will disambiguate. If (A), using OLMo/Qwen reference fixes it; if (B), the signal genuinely doesn't exist for these families. In worst tier, we expect (B) to dominate. Narrative must pivot to conditional claims.\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设在此暴露：2+ 新家族 held-out F1 < 0.60。Pythia 家族内 transfer 良好（两个 Pythia 模型互相泄露 inductive bias），但 OLMo 和 Qwen 家族 held-out 时 binary F1 掉到 0.57-0.58。原因：(1) OLMo 的 training recipe（Dolma corpus + unique LR schedule）产生不同的 token frequency distribution，导致 Pythia-410M reference model 的 entropy features 对 OLMo 生成文本的 depth drift 不敏感——entropy_mean 的 Spearman 仅 -0.22（vs Pythia -0.61），effect size 缩小 2.8x；(2) Qwen tokenizer 完全不同（byte-level BPE vs Pythia GPT-NeoX tokenizer），surface features（TTR/hapax）的计算基于不同 vocabulary space，导致跨家族 surface feature 分布 mismatch；(3) full vs surface-only 差距仅 2pp（0.72 vs 0.70），McNemar p=0.12 不显著——7-feature ensemble 在这个场景下不优于简单 surface features，印证 'seven_feat_vs_best_baseline_pp: [0, 2.0]' 的 worst 预期。per_gen_f1_std = 0.11 远高于 'universal' 叙事所需的一致性。\"\n290\t  },\n291\t  {\n292\t    \"name\": \"paraphrastic_comparison\",\n293\t    \"description\": \"Paraphrasing chains vs continuation chains 直接对比，测试 attractor convergence 理论\",\n294\t    \"results\": {\n295\t      \"paraphrastic_3class_f1\": 0.6,\n296\t      \"paraphrastic_binary_f1\": 0.53,\n297\t      \"continuation_3class_f1\": 0.72,\n298\t      \"continuation_binary_f1\": 0.67,\n299\t      \"f1_3class_delta\": -0.12,\n300\t      \"spearman_entropy_mean_para\": 0.15,\n301\t      \"spearman_entropy_mean_cont\": -0.42,\n302\t      \"spearman_ttr_para\": 0.31,\n303\t      \"spearman_ttr_cont\": -0.48,\n304\t      \"spearman_hapax_para\": 0.28,\n305\t      \"spearman_hapax_cont\": -0.51,\n306\t      \"cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1\": 0.38,\n307\t      \"cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1\": 0.42,\n308\t      \"depth_retention_para\": 0.92,\n309\t      \"depth_retention_cont\": 0.83,\n310\t      \"para_attractor_convergence_gen3\": true,\n311\t      \"n_paraphrastic\": 4800,\n312\t      \"n_continuation\": 4600\n313\t    },\n314\t    \"tables\": [\n315\t      {\n316\t        \"name\": \"Table: Paraphrastic vs Continuation Depth Signal\",\n317\t        \"columns\": [\n318\t          \"Metric\",\n319\t          \"Paraphrastic\",\n320\t          \"Continuation\",\n321\t          \"Delta\"\n322\t        ],\n323\t        \"rows\": [\n324\t          [\n325\t            \"3-class LOGO F1\",\n326\t            0.6,\n327\t            0.72,\n328\t            -0.12\n329\t          ],\n330\t          [\n331\t            \"Binary LOGO F1\",\n332\t            0.53,\n333\t            0.67,\n334\t            -0.14\n335\t          ],\n336\t          [\n337\t            \"ρ(entropy_mean, depth)\",\n338\t            \"+0.15\",\n339\t            \"-0.42\",\n340\t            \"sign reversed\"\n341\t          ],\n342\t          [\n343\t            \"ρ(TTR, depth)\",\n344\t            \"+0.31\",\n345\t            \"-0.48\",\n346\t            \"sign reversed\"\n347\t          ],\n348\t          [\n349\t            \"ρ(hapax, depth)\",\n350\t            \"+0.28\",\n351\t            \"-0.51\",\n352\t            \"sign reversed\"\n353\t          ],\n354\t          [\n355\t            \"Depth retention (gen4/gen0)\",\n356\t            0.92,\n357\t            0.83,\n358\t            \"+0.09\"\n359\t          ]\n360\t        ]\n361\t      },\n362\t      {\n363\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-transfer LOGO F1\",\n364\t        \"columns\": [\n365\t          \"Train on\",\n366\t          \"Test on\",\n367\t          \"F1\"\n368\t        ],\n369\t        \"rows\": [\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"Continuation\",\n372\t            \"Continuation\",\n373\t            0.72\n374\t          ],\n375\t          [\n376\t            \"Paraphrastic\",\n377\t            \"Paraphrastic\",\n378\t            0.6\n379\t          ],\n380\t          [\n381\t            \"Continuation → Para\",\n382\t            \"Paraphrastic\",\n383\t            0.42\n384\t          ],\n385\t          [\n386\t            \"Para → Continuation\",\n387\t            \"Continuation\",\n388\t            0.38\n389\t          ]\n390\t        ]\n391\t      }\n392\t    ],\n393\t    \"figures\": [],\n394\t    \"analysis\": \"Sign reversal confirms theoretically expected behavior (paraphrasing → attractor convergence, continuation → monotonic drift), but under worst tier the effect sizes are underwhelming for both types. Paraphrastic binary F1=0.53 is near random — essentially unclassifiable beyond gen-0 vs rest. Continuation is better but still weak (0.67 binary). The low cross-transfer (0.38-0.42) means there's no unified 'depth signal' that works across chain types — each requires its own model. For EMNLP reframing: this SUPPORTS the 'architecture-conditional' narrative because it shows depth signal properties depend on the specific generation process (paraphrasing vs continuation vs architecture), not just depth itself. The attractor convergence finding is a positive contribution to theory validation even in worst case.\\n\\nWorst 档下，paraphrastic chains 呈现 attractor convergence 预期行为：entropy_mean Spearman 仅 +0.15（趋于 neutral/轻微 positive，即 paraphrasing 使 perplexity 略微上升后稳定）。但 continuation chains 也弱于 expected——在 5-gen pooled data 上 Spearman 仅 -0.42（而非 best 档的 -0.65+），因为 non-Pythia generators 拉低了整体 correlation。关键是 sign reversal：paraphrastic 正相关 vs continuation 负相关，但 effect size 都不大。Cross-transfer F1 极低（0.38-0.42），说明两种 chain 类型的 feature space 几乎不重叠——这在 worst 档是问题而非 feature，因为它意味着 'depth signal' 高度 task-specific，不是一个 unified phenomenon。Depth retention 0.92 for para（高于 continuation 的 0.83）也 counterintuitive：paraphrasing 保留更多 chains 但 signal 更弱，说明 chain stability ≠ signal strength。Attractor convergence 在 gen-3 后明显——para chains 的 feature 分布停止变化。\"\n395\t  },\n396\t  {\n397\t    \"name\": \"finer_grained_ordinal\",\n398\t    \"description\": \"5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4) 测试更细粒度深度估计\",\n399\t    \"results\": {\n400\t      \"5class_macro_f1\": 0.38,\n401\t      \"5class_f1_std\": 0.04,\n402\t      \"5class_accuracy\": 0.42,\n403\t      \"5class_mae\": 0.95,\n404\t      \"3class_macro_f1\": 0.72,\n405\t      \"delta_5class_vs_3class\": -0.34,\n406\t      \"per_class_f1\": {\n407\t        \"depth_0\": 0.85,\n408\t        \"depth_1\": 0.45,\n409\t        \"depth_2\": 0.22,\n410\t        \"depth_3\": 0.18,\n411\t        \"depth_4\": 0.2\n412\t      },\n413\t      \"confusion_concentration\": \"gen2/gen3/gen4 互相混淆，占 confusion matrix off-diagonal 的 72%\",\n414\t      \"ordinal_methods\": {\n415\t        \"CORAL\": 0.36,\n416\t        \"frank_hall\": 0.39,\n417\t        \"xgboost\": 0.38\n418\t      },\n419\t      \"depth_2_3_separability\": \"Cohen's d = 0.08 (entropy_mean), 0.12 (hapax_ratio) — 几乎不可分\",\n420\t      \"per_family_5class\": {\n421\t        \"pythia_held_out\": 0.48,\n422\t        \"olmo_held_out\": 0.28,\n423\t        \"qwen_held_out\": 0.31\n424\t      }\n425\t    },\n426\t    \"tables\": [\n427\t      {\n428\t        \"name\": \"Table: Ordinal Classification Results\",\n429\t        \"columns\": [\n430\t          \"Granularity\",\n431\t          \"Method\",\n432\t          \"Macro F1\",\n433\t          \"MAE\"\n434\t        ],\n435\t        \"rows\": [\n436\t          [\n437\t            \"3-class\",\n438\t            \"XGBoost\",\n439\t            0.72,\n440\t            0.31\n441\t          ],\n442\t          [\n443\t            \"5-class\",\n444\t            \"XGBoost\",\n445\t            0.38,\n446\t            0.95\n447\t          ],\n448\t          [\n449\t            \"5-class\",\n450\t            \"CORAL\",\n451\t            0.36,\n452\t            0.98\n453\t          ],\n454\t          [\n455\t            \"5-class\",\n456\t            \"Frank-Hall\",\n457\t            0.39,\n458\t            0.92\n459\t          ]\n460\t        ]\n461\t      },\n462\t      {\n463\t        \"name\": \"Table: 5-class Per-depth F1\",\n464\t        \"columns\": [\n465\t          \"Depth\",\n466\t          \"F1\",\n467\t          \"Support\",\n468\t          \"Most confused with\"\n469\t        ],\n470\t        \"rows\": [\n471\t          [\n472\t            \"gen-0\",\n473\t            0.85,\n474\t            4950,\n475\t            \"gen-1 (10%)\"\n476\t          ],\n477\t          [\n478\t            \"gen-1\",\n479\t            0.45,\n480\t            4900,\n481\t            \"gen-2 (28%)\"\n482\t          ],\n483\t          [\n484\t            \"gen-2\",\n485\t            0.22,\n486\t            4600,\n487\t            \"gen-3 (35%), gen-1 (22%)\"\n488\t          ],\n489\t          [\n490\t            \"gen-3\",\n491\t            0.18,\n492\t            4200,\n493\t            \"gen-2 (33%), gen-4 (30%)\"\n494\t          ],\n495\t          [\n496\t            \"gen-4\",\n497\t            0.2,\n498\t            3800,\n499\t            \"gen-3 (38%), gen-2 (21%)\"\n500\t          ]\n501\t        ]\n502\t      }\n503\t    ],\n504\t    \"figures\": [],\n505\t    \"analysis\": \"5-class ordinal is infeasible in worst tier. The signal exists primarily at the gen-0/gen-1 boundary and rapidly degrades. This is actually informative for the reframed paper: it establishes an empirical ceiling on depth resolution (≤3 classes) that's architecture-dependent. For Pythia-family generators where signal is strong, 4-class might work; for others, even binary (gen-1 vs gen-2+) is near chance. The 'conditions under which depth signal emerges vs collapses' framing gains direct evidence: depth granularity is architecture-conditional, not a universal property of recursive generation. Report as structured negative finding.\\n\\nWorst 档下，5-class 在 pooled 5-gen data 上 macro F1 仅 0.38，接近 5-class random baseline（0.20）但仍显著高于 chance。核心问题：depth 2/3/4 几乎不可分（per-class F1 0.18-0.22）。原因是双重的：(1) depth drift 在多数生成器（OLMo/Qwen）上本身就弱，加上 (2) gen-2 到 gen-4 之间的 feature 增量极小（Cohen's d < 0.12），即使在 Pythia 上也进入 plateau。只有 gen-0 可靠分类（F1=0.85），gen-1 中等（0.45）——这本质上是 binary detection（gen-0 vs rest）在 5-class 框架中的残影。OLMo/Qwen held-out 时 5-class F1 掉到 0.28-0.31（接近 random），进一步说明 fine-grained 深度估计只在特定架构下可行。Ordinal-specific methods（CORAL/Frank-Hall）无优势，因为 underlying signal 本身不存在于 deep depths。3-class（0.72）远优于 5-class（0.38），但 delta = 34pp 说明 3-class 的性能也主要来自 gen-0 classification 而非真正的 ordinal discrimination。\"\n506\t  },\n507\t  {\n508\t    \"name\": \"end_to_end_classifier\",\n509\t    \"description\": \"QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3.5-0.8B 端到端深度分类，对比 handcrafted features\",\n510\t    \"results\": {\n511\t      \"5class_macro_f1\": 0.44,\n512\t      \"5class_f1_std\": 0.02,\n513\t      \"3class_macro_f1\": 0.76,\n514\t      \"3class_f1_std\": 0.01,\n515\t      \"per_class_f1\": {\n516\t        \"gen0\": 0.95,\n517\t        \"gen1\": 0.62,\n518\t        \"gen2\": 0.3,\n519\t        \"gen3\": 0.22,\n520\t        \"gen4\": 0.11\n521\t      },\n522\t      \"vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp\": \"+6.0\",\n523\t      \"vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp\": \"+4.0\",\n524\t      \"logo_generalization\": {\n525\t        \"pythia_held_out\": 0.52,\n526\t        \"olmo_held_out\": 0.35,\n527\t        \"qwen_held_out\": 0.38\n528\t      },\n529\t      \"overfitting_gap\": 0.18,\n530\t      \"train_f1\": 0.62,\n531\t      \"val_f1\": 0.44,\n532\t      \"runtime_hours\": 14,\n533\t      \"model\": \"Qwen3-0.6B-Base\",\n534\t      \"method\": \"QLoRA rank-16\"\n535\t    },\n536\t    \"tables\": [\n537\t      {\n538\t        \"name\": \"Table: E2E vs Handcrafted Features\",\n539\t        \"columns\": [\n540\t          \"Method\",\n541\t          \"5-class F1\",\n542\t          \"3-class F1\",\n543\t          \"LOGO 5-class F1\"\n544\t        ],\n545\t        \"rows\": [\n546\t          [\n547\t            \"XGBoost 7-feature\",\n548\t            0.38,\n549\t            0.72,\n550\t            0.34\n551\t          ],\n552\t          [\n553\t            \"QLoRA Qwen3-0.6B\",\n554\t            0.44,\n555\t            0.76,\n556\t            0.38\n557\t          ],\n558\t          [\n559\t            \"Delta\",\n560\t            \"+0.06\",\n561\t            \"+0.04\",\n562\t            \"+0.04\"\n563\t          ]\n564\t        ]\n565\t      },\n566\t      {\n567\t        \"name\": \"Table: QLoRA LOGO Per-family Held-out\",\n568\t        \"columns\": [\n569\t          \"Held-out Family\",\n570\t          \"5-class F1\",\n571\t          \"Overfitting gap\"\n572\t        ],\n573\t        \"rows\": [\n574\t          [\n575\t            \"Pythia (2.8B+1B)\",\n576\t            0.52,\n577\t            0.1\n578\t          ],\n579\t          [\n580\t            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n581\t            0.35,\n582\t            0.27\n583\t          ],\n584\t          [\n585\t            \"Qwen (1.7B+0.6B)\",\n586\t            0.38,\n587\t            0.24\n588\t          ]\n589\t        ]\n590\t      }\n591\t    ],\n592\t    \"figures\": [],\n593\t    \"analysis\": \"E2E model provides modest improvement over handcrafted features but does not solve the fundamental problem: depth signal for non-Pythia architectures is weak or absent. The overfitting pattern (generator-specific memorization) is actually diagnostic evidence for the reframed paper: it shows that whatever distinguishes depths for a given generator is not transferable across architectures. This supports the 'architecture-conditional depth response' thesis — each model family has its own depth signature (if any), and there is no universal learned representation of 'depth'. For the paper: report as supplementary evidence that neither handcrafted nor learned features achieve universal depth discrimination, strengthening the conditional-claim reframing.\\n\\nE2E model 在 5-class 上优于 XGBoost（0.44 vs 0.38，+6pp），因为 learned representations 能捕获 handcrafted features 遗漏的 subtle patterns（如 attention pattern shifts、specific n-gram frequency changes）。但绝对性能仍然很差（0.44），且 overfitting 严重（train 0.62 vs val 0.44，gap=18pp）——模型学到了 generator-specific artifacts 而非 generalizable depth signal。LOGO generalization 更加灾难性：held-out Pythia F1=0.52，OLMo/Qwen 仅 0.35-0.38。这说明 E2E model 学到的不是 'depth signal' 而是 'generator fingerprint + depth 交互'——它在训练集内的 generator 上过拟合。3-class（0.76）优于 XGBoost（0.72）但差距不大（+4pp），且同样来自 gen-0 classification。在 worst 档下，E2E 的相对优势说明确实有 beyond-handcrafted-features 的信号存在，但这些信号 generator-specific、不泛化，支持 'architecture-conditional' reframing。\"\n594\t  }\n595\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"964b1302-a184-44d7-b569-2d485d8ffbd0","uuid":"fb5200b8-f0e8-4dee-bb29-2cf2b3a135f4","timestamp":"2026-05-16T16:14:53.168Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_3/projects/gen-depth-fingerprint/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T155725/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"feature_ablation_and_trend\",\n    \"description\": \"MVP Pythia-only 数据上的特征消融 + 趋势分析 + perplexity 预验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"full_macro_f1\": 0.81,\n      \"reference_only_f1\": 0.68,\n      \"surface_only_f1\": 0.77,\n      \"ref_vs_surf_bootstrap_p\": 0.003,\n      \"h2_features\": \"entropy_mean (slope=-0.42, R²=0.88), ttr (slope=-0.11, R²=0.91), hapax_ratio (slope=-0.14, R²=0.93)\",\n      \"h1_features\": \"tail_decay (slope=-0.02, R²=0.15), entropy_std (slope=+0.01, R²=0.08), entropy_max (slope=-0.06, R²=0.31), entropy_min (slope=-0.09, R²=0.42)\",\n      \"entropy_min_ambiguous\": true,\n      \"median_ppl_by_depth\": \"13.2, 5.1, 3.2, 2.3, 1.8\",\n      \"ppl_depth_spearman\": -0.95\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Feature Ablation (5-fold CV, Pythia-2.8B only)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Feature Set\",\n          \"Macro F1\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Full 7-feature\",\n            0.81,\n            \"[0.79, 0.83]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Surface only (TTR + hapax)\",\n            0.77,\n            \"[0.75, 0.79]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Reference only (5 entropy feats)\",\n            0.68,\n            \"[0.65, 0.71]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_mean alone\",\n            0.64,\n            \"[0.61, 0.67]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Linear Trend per Feature (depth 0-4)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Feature\",\n          \"Slope\",\n          \"R²\",\n          \"Classification\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"hapax_ratio\",\n            -0.14,\n            0.93,\n            \"Drifting\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ttr\",\n            -0.11,\n            0.91,\n            \"Drifting\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_mean\",\n            -0.42,\n            0.88,\n            \"Drifting\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_min\",\n            -0.09,\n            0.42,\n            \"Ambiguous\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_max\",\n            -0.06,\n            0.31,\n            \"Stationary\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"tail_decay\",\n            -0.02,\n            0.15,\n            \"Stationary\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"entropy_std\",\n            0.01,\n            0.08,\n            \"Stationary\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Initial signal looks promising on same-family data but two warning signs: (1) surface features dominate reference features by 9pp, suggesting vocabulary impoverishment is the primary signal carrier, not distributional structure shifts; (2) entropy_min sits in an ambiguous zone. In worst tier these are early indicators that the 'dual dynamics' framework is architecture-specific — it cleanly separates on Pythia but may not generalize. Proceed to plan_002 but with lowered expectations for cross-family transfer.\\n\\nPythia-410M reference + Pythia-2.8B generator 是 same-family 最佳条件，即使在 worst 档位下初始 MVP 数据仍然能看到 depth signal。问题不在这里暴露——surface features（TTR/hapax）占主导（0.77 vs ref-only 0.68）暗示 depth signal 主要来自 vocabulary impoverishment 而非深层 distributional structure。entropy_min 的 R²=0.42 处于模糊地带（不完全 stationary），为后续 cross-family 失败埋下伏笔：这种 intermediate behavior 说明 drifting/stationary 分界在不同架构下可能不一致。Reference features 弱于 surface 是 worst 档早期信号——如果 dual dynamics 是 robust phenomenon，reference features 应至少持平。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_generator_evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"5 生成器 (Pythia-2.8B/1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B) LOGO 交叉验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_records\": 18200,\n      \"logo_avg_macro_f1_3class\": 0.72,\n      \"logo_avg_binary_f1\": 0.67,\n      \"logo_per_generator\": {\n        \"pythia-2.8b\": {\n          \"3class\": 0.82,\n          \"binary\": 0.78\n        },\n        \"pythia-1b\": {\n          \"3class\": 0.84,\n          \"binary\": 0.8\n        },\n        \"olmo-2-1b\": {\n          \"3class\": 0.63,\n          \"binary\": 0.58\n        },\n        \"qwen3-1.7b\": {\n          \"3class\": 0.67,\n          \"binary\": 0.62\n        },\n        \"qwen3-0.6b\": {\n          \"3class\": 0.64,\n          \"binary\": 0.57\n        }\n      },\n      \"per_gen_f1_std\": 0.11,\n      \"leave_one_family_out\": {\n        \"held_out_pythia\": 0.79,\n        \"held_out_olmo\": 0.58,\n        \"held_out_qwen\": 0.6\n      },\n      \"ablation_full_f1\": 0.72,\n      \"ablation_surface_only_f1\": 0.7,\n      \"ablation_reference_only_f1\": 0.61,\n      \"mcnemar_full_vs_surface_p\": 0.12,\n      \"generators_below_060_binary\": 2,\n      \"spearman_by_generator\": {\n        \"pythia-2.8b\": {\n          \"entropy_mean\": -0.61,\n          \"ttr\": -0.58,\n          \"hapax\": -0.63\n        },\n        \"pythia-1b\": {\n          \"entropy_mean\": -0.55,\n          \"ttr\": -0.54,\n          \"hapax\": -0.6\n        },\n        \"olmo-2-1b\": {\n          \"entropy_mean\": -0.22,\n          \"ttr\": -0.35,\n          \"hapax\": -0.38\n        },\n        \"qwen3-1.7b\": {\n          \"entropy_mean\": -0.31,\n          \"ttr\": -0.4,\n          \"hapax\": -0.43\n        },\n        \"qwen3-0.6b\": {\n          \"entropy_mean\": -0.18,\n          \"ttr\": -0.33,\n          \"hapax\": -0.36\n        }\n      },\n      \"feature_direction_inconsistency\": \"OLMo entropy_mean correlation weakly negative (-0.22) while Pythia strongly negative (-0.61); effect size ratio 2.8x\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: LOGO Cross-Generator Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Held-out Generator\",\n          \"3-class F1\",\n          \"Binary F1\",\n          \"Family\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pythia-2.8B\",\n            0.82,\n            0.78,\n            \"Pythia\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pythia-1B\",\n            0.84,\n            0.8,\n            \"Pythia\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n            0.63,\n            0.58,\n            \"OLMo\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n            0.67,\n            0.62,\n            \"Qwen\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-0.6B\",\n            0.64,\n            0.57,\n            \"Qwen\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"**Average**\",\n            \"**0.72**\",\n            \"**0.67**\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Feature Ablation (5-gen LOGO)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Feature Set\",\n          \"Avg LOGO F1\",\n          \"p vs Full\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Full 7-feature\",\n            0.72,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Surface only\",\n            0.7,\n            \"0.12 (NS)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Reference only\",\n            0.61,\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Spearman ρ (entropy_mean vs depth) by Generator\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Generator\",\n          \"ρ\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Effect interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pythia-2.8B\",\n            -0.61,\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"Strong\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pythia-1B\",\n            -0.55,\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"Moderate-Strong\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n            -0.31,\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"Weak-Moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-0.6B\",\n            -0.18,\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"Weak\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n            -0.22,\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"Weak\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Universality claim collapses. The 2-tier pattern (Pythia strong, others weak) indicates depth signal is not an intrinsic property of recursive generation but depends on architecture/training-data alignment with the reference model AND possibly on the generator's own sampling dynamics. Two interpretations: (A) reference model mismatch — Pythia-410M is a poor scorer for non-Pythia text, inflating entropy baseline and suppressing drift measurement; (B) genuine architecture difference — some models produce more uniform token distributions at every depth, compressing the dynamic range for drift detection. Plan_003 (cross-family reference) will disambiguate. If (A), using OLMo/Qwen reference fixes it; if (B), the signal genuinely doesn't exist for these families. In worst tier, we expect (B) to dominate. Narrative must pivot to conditional claims.\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设在此暴露：2+ 新家族 held-out F1 < 0.60。Pythia 家族内 transfer 良好（两个 Pythia 模型互相泄露 inductive bias），但 OLMo 和 Qwen 家族 held-out 时 binary F1 掉到 0.57-0.58。原因：(1) OLMo 的 training recipe（Dolma corpus + unique LR schedule）产生不同的 token frequency distribution，导致 Pythia-410M reference model 的 entropy features 对 OLMo 生成文本的 depth drift 不敏感——entropy_mean 的 Spearman 仅 -0.22（vs Pythia -0.61），effect size 缩小 2.8x；(2) Qwen tokenizer 完全不同（byte-level BPE vs Pythia GPT-NeoX tokenizer），surface features（TTR/hapax）的计算基于不同 vocabulary space，导致跨家族 surface feature 分布 mismatch；(3) full vs surface-only 差距仅 2pp（0.72 vs 0.70），McNemar p=0.12 不显著——7-feature ensemble 在这个场景下不优于简单 surface features，印证 'seven_feat_vs_best_baseline_pp: [0, 2.0]' 的 worst 预期。per_gen_f1_std = 0.11 远高于 'universal' 叙事所需的一致性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"paraphrastic_comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Paraphrasing chains vs continuation chains 直接对比，测试 attractor convergence 理论\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"paraphrastic_3class_f1\": 0.6,\n      \"paraphrastic_binary_f1\": 0.53,\n      \"continuation_3class_f1\": 0.72,\n      \"continuation_binary_f1\": 0.67,\n      \"f1_3class_delta\": -0.12,\n      \"spearman_entropy_mean_para\": 0.15,\n      \"spearman_entropy_mean_cont\": -0.42,\n      \"spearman_ttr_para\": 0.31,\n      \"spearman_ttr_cont\": -0.48,\n      \"spearman_hapax_para\": 0.28,\n      \"spearman_hapax_cont\": -0.51,\n      \"cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1\": 0.38,\n      \"cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1\": 0.42,\n      \"depth_retention_para\": 0.92,\n      \"depth_retention_cont\": 0.83,\n      \"para_attractor_convergence_gen3\": true,\n      \"n_paraphrastic\": 4800,\n      \"n_continuation\": 4600\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Paraphrastic vs Continuation Depth Signal\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Paraphrastic\",\n          \"Continuation\",\n          \"Delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"3-class LOGO F1\",\n            0.6,\n            0.72,\n            -0.12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binary LOGO F1\",\n            0.53,\n            0.67,\n            -0.14\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ρ(entropy_mean, depth)\",\n            \"+0.15\",\n            \"-0.42\",\n            \"sign reversed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ρ(TTR, depth)\",\n            \"+0.31\",\n            \"-0.48\",\n            \"sign reversed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ρ(hapax, depth)\",\n            \"+0.28\",\n            \"-0.51\",\n            \"sign reversed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Depth retention (gen4/gen0)\",\n            0.92,\n            0.83,\n            \"+0.09\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-transfer LOGO F1\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Train on\",\n          \"Test on\",\n          \"F1\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Continuation\",\n            \"Continuation\",\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Paraphrastic\",\n            \"Paraphrastic\",\n            0.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Continuation → Para\",\n            \"Paraphrastic\",\n            0.42\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Para → Continuation\",\n            \"Continuation\",\n            0.38\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Sign reversal confirms theoretically expected behavior (paraphrasing → attractor convergence, continuation → monotonic drift), but under worst tier the effect sizes are underwhelming for both types. Paraphrastic binary F1=0.53 is near random — essentially unclassifiable beyond gen-0 vs rest. Continuation is better but still weak (0.67 binary). The low cross-transfer (0.38-0.42) means there's no unified 'depth signal' that works across chain types — each requires its own model. For EMNLP reframing: this SUPPORTS the 'architecture-conditional' narrative because it shows depth signal properties depend on the specific generation process (paraphrasing vs continuation vs architecture), not just depth itself. The attractor convergence finding is a positive contribution to theory validation even in worst case.\\n\\nWorst 档下，paraphrastic chains 呈现 attractor convergence 预期行为：entropy_mean Spearman 仅 +0.15（趋于 neutral/轻微 positive，即 paraphrasing 使 perplexity 略微上升后稳定）。但 continuation chains 也弱于 expected——在 5-gen pooled data 上 Spearman 仅 -0.42（而非 best 档的 -0.65+），因为 non-Pythia generators 拉低了整体 correlation。关键是 sign reversal：paraphrastic 正相关 vs continuation 负相关，但 effect size 都不大。Cross-transfer F1 极低（0.38-0.42），说明两种 chain 类型的 feature space 几乎不重叠——这在 worst 档是问题而非 feature，因为它意味着 'depth signal' 高度 task-specific，不是一个 unified phenomenon。Depth retention 0.92 for para（高于 continuation 的 0.83）也 counterintuitive：paraphrasing 保留更多 chains 但 signal 更弱，说明 chain stability ≠ signal strength。Attractor convergence 在 gen-3 后明显——para chains 的 feature 分布停止变化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"finer_grained_ordinal\",\n    \"description\": \"5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4) 测试更细粒度深度估计\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"5class_macro_f1\": 0.38,\n      \"5class_f1_std\": 0.04,\n      \"5class_accuracy\": 0.42,\n      \"5class_mae\": 0.95,\n      \"3class_macro_f1\": 0.72,\n      \"delta_5class_vs_3class\": -0.34,\n      \"per_class_f1\": {\n        \"depth_0\": 0.85,\n        \"depth_1\": 0.45,\n        \"depth_2\": 0.22,\n        \"depth_3\": 0.18,\n        \"depth_4\": 0.2\n      },\n      \"confusion_concentration\": \"gen2/gen3/gen4 互相混淆，占 confusion matrix off-diagonal 的 72%\",\n      \"ordinal_methods\": {\n        \"CORAL\": 0.36,\n        \"frank_hall\": 0.39,\n        \"xgboost\": 0.38\n      },\n      \"depth_2_3_separability\": \"Cohen's d = 0.08 (entropy_mean), 0.12 (hapax_ratio) — 几乎不可分\",\n      \"per_family_5class\": {\n        \"pythia_held_out\": 0.48,\n        \"olmo_held_out\": 0.28,\n        \"qwen_held_out\": 0.31\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Ordinal Classification Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Granularity\",\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Macro F1\",\n          \"MAE\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"3-class\",\n            \"XGBoost\",\n            0.72,\n            0.31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5-class\",\n            \"XGBoost\",\n            0.38,\n            0.95\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5-class\",\n            \"CORAL\",\n            0.36,\n            0.98\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5-class\",\n            \"Frank-Hall\",\n            0.39,\n            0.92\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 5-class Per-depth F1\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Depth\",\n          \"F1\",\n          \"Support\",\n          \"Most confused with\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"gen-0\",\n            0.85,\n            4950,\n            \"gen-1 (10%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-1\",\n            0.45,\n            4900,\n            \"gen-2 (28%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-2\",\n            0.22,\n            4600,\n            \"gen-3 (35%), gen-1 (22%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-3\",\n            0.18,\n            4200,\n            \"gen-2 (33%), gen-4 (30%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gen-4\",\n            0.2,\n            3800,\n            \"gen-3 (38%), gen-2 (21%)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"5-class ordinal is infeasible in worst tier. The signal exists primarily at the gen-0/gen-1 boundary and rapidly degrades. This is actually informative for the reframed paper: it establishes an empirical ceiling on depth resolution (≤3 classes) that's architecture-dependent. For Pythia-family generators where signal is strong, 4-class might work; for others, even binary (gen-1 vs gen-2+) is near chance. The 'conditions under which depth signal emerges vs collapses' framing gains direct evidence: depth granularity is architecture-conditional, not a universal property of recursive generation. Report as structured negative finding.\\n\\nWorst 档下，5-class 在 pooled 5-gen data 上 macro F1 仅 0.38，接近 5-class random baseline（0.20）但仍显著高于 chance。核心问题：depth 2/3/4 几乎不可分（per-class F1 0.18-0.22）。原因是双重的：(1) depth drift 在多数生成器（OLMo/Qwen）上本身就弱，加上 (2) gen-2 到 gen-4 之间的 feature 增量极小（Cohen's d < 0.12），即使在 Pythia 上也进入 plateau。只有 gen-0 可靠分类（F1=0.85），gen-1 中等（0.45）——这本质上是 binary detection（gen-0 vs rest）在 5-class 框架中的残影。OLMo/Qwen held-out 时 5-class F1 掉到 0.28-0.31（接近 random），进一步说明 fine-grained 深度估计只在特定架构下可行。Ordinal-specific methods（CORAL/Frank-Hall）无优势，因为 underlying signal 本身不存在于 deep depths。3-class（0.72）远优于 5-class（0.38），但 delta = 34pp 说明 3-class 的性能也主要来自 gen-0 classification 而非真正的 ordinal discrimination。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"end_to_end_classifier\",\n    \"description\": \"QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3.5-0.8B 端到端深度分类，对比 handcrafted features\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"5class_macro_f1\": 0.44,\n      \"5class_f1_std\": 0.02,\n      \"3class_macro_f1\": 0.76,\n      \"3class_f1_std\": 0.01,\n      \"per_class_f1\": {\n        \"gen0\": 0.95,\n        \"gen1\": 0.62,\n        \"gen2\": 0.3,\n        \"gen3\": 0.22,\n        \"gen4\": 0.11\n      },\n      \"vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp\": \"+6.0\",\n      \"vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp\": \"+4.0\",\n      \"logo_generalization\": {\n        \"pythia_held_out\": 0.52,\n        \"olmo_held_out\": 0.35,\n        \"qwen_held_out\": 0.38\n      },\n      \"overfitting_gap\": 0.18,\n      \"train_f1\": 0.62,\n      \"val_f1\": 0.44,\n      \"runtime_hours\": 14,\n      \"model\": \"Qwen3-0.6B-Base\",\n      \"method\": \"QLoRA rank-16\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: E2E vs Handcrafted Features\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"5-class F1\",\n          \"3-class F1\",\n          \"LOGO 5-class F1\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"XGBoost 7-feature\",\n            0.38,\n            0.72,\n            0.34\n          ],\n          [\n            \"QLoRA Qwen3-0.6B\",\n            0.44,\n            0.76,\n            0.38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Delta\",\n            \"+0.06\",\n            \"+0.04\",\n            \"+0.04\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: QLoRA LOGO Per-family Held-out\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Held-out Family\",\n          \"5-class F1\",\n          \"Overfitting gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pythia (2.8B+1B)\",\n            0.52,\n            0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OLMo-2-1B\",\n            0.35,\n            0.27\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen (1.7B+0.6B)\",\n            0.38,\n            0.24\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"E2E model provides modest improvement over handcrafted features but does not solve the fundamental problem: depth signal for non-Pythia architectures is weak or absent. The overfitting pattern (generator-specific memorization) is actually diagnostic evidence for the reframed paper: it shows that whatever distinguishes depths for a given generator is not transferable across architectures. This supports the 'architecture-conditional depth response' thesis — each model family has its own depth signature (if any), and there is no universal learned representation of 'depth'. For the paper: report as supplementary evidence that neither handcrafted nor learned features achieve universal depth discrimination, strengthening the conditional-claim reframing.\\n\\nE2E model 在 5-class 上优于 XGBoost（0.44 vs 0.38，+6pp），因为 learned representations 能捕获 handcrafted features 遗漏的 subtle patterns（如 attention pattern shifts、specific n-gram frequency changes）。但绝对性能仍然很差（0.44），且 overfitting 严重（train 0.62 vs val 0.44，gap=18pp）——模型学到了 generator-specific artifacts 而非 generalizable depth signal。LOGO generalization 更加灾难性：held-out Pythia F1=0.52，OLMo/Qwen 仅 0.35-0.38。这说明 E2E model 学到的不是 'depth signal' 而是 'generator fingerprint + depth 交互'——它在训练集内的 generator 上过拟合。3-class（0.76）优于 XGBoost（0.72）但差距不大（+4pp），且同样来自 gen-0 classification。在 worst 档下，E2E 的相对优势说明确实有 beyond-handcrafted-features 的信号存在，但这些信号 generator-specific、不泛化，支持 'architecture-conditional' reframing。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":595,"startLine":1,"totalLines":595}}}
